        "salon-and-beauty-services": "---\nslug: salon-and-beauty-services\ntype: trade\nname: Salon and beauty services\nline: The rate, the SAC codes and a sample invoice.\ntopic: salon and beauty services\nsearch: gst on salon services\ntitle: \"GST on salon services: rate, SAC code and invoice\"\ndescription: \"GST on salon services: the rate since 22 Sep 2025, the SAC codes for hair and beauty, and a sample invoice with the split worked out.\"\nh1: \"GST on salon and beauty services: rate, SAC code and a sample invoice\"\nanswer: \"Salon, barber and beauty services are taxed at **5% GST, without input tax credit**, since 22 Sep 2025. It was 18% before. Within your state that's CGST 2.5% + SGST 2.5%.\"\nupdated: 2026-10-24\ncheckedOn: 2026-10-24\nauthor:\n  name: Saroh team\n  role: Writer\ncodes:\n  - kind: SAC\n    code: \"999721\"\n    label: hairdressing and barbers\n    rate: 5\n  - kind: SAC\n    code: \"999722\"\n    label: cosmetic treatment, manicure, pedicure\n    rate: 5\nfacts:\n  - label: Rate\n    value: 5%\n    note: without input tax credit\n  - label: \"SAC: hair\"\n    value: \"999721\"\n    note: hairdressing and barbers\n  - label: \"SAC: beauty\"\n    value: \"999722\"\n    note: cosmetic treatment, manicure, pedicure\n  - label: In your state\n    value: CGST 2.5% + SGST 2.5%\n    note: \"another state: IGST 5%\"\ntable:\n  kind: invoice\n  title: A sample invoice\n  head: [Service, SAC, Value, CGST 2.5%, SGST 2.5%, Total]\n  rows:\n    - [Haircut and blow-dry (women), \"999721\", \"₹800.00\", \"₹20.00\", \"₹20.00\", \"₹840.00\"]\n    - [D-Tan facial, \"999722\", \"₹1,500.00\", \"₹37.50\", \"₹37.50\", \"₹1,575.00\"]\n  foot: [Total, \"\", \"₹2,300.00\", \"₹57.50\", \"₹57.50\", \"₹2,415.00\"]\n  note: Gulmohar Unisex Salon in Koramangala, Bengaluru, and a customer in Bengaluru. Worked out with the same rules Saroh's own invoices use.\nsources:\n  - label: the CBIC rate notification for services in force from 22 Sep 2025\n    href: https://cbic-gst.gov.in/\nmistakes:\n  - title: Still charging 18%.\n    body: \"Check your billing software and printed rate cards: the rate for salon services has been 5% since 22 Sep 2025.\"\n  - title: Claiming input tax credit.\n    body: At 5% for these services, the credit isn't available.\n  - title: One line for a service and a product.\n    body: Bill a facial and the serum you sold with it on separate lines, each at its own rate.\nquestions:\n  - question: Do I need to charge GST if I'm not registered?\n    answer: No, and you mustn't. A business that isn't registered can't collect GST; it gives a plain bill with no tax.\n  - question: Is GST different for products I sell in the salon?\n    answer: Yes. Products go at the rate for their HSN code, on their own line.\n  - question: What about a deposit taken at booking?\n    answer: GST on a service is due when you receive the payment, so a deposit carries GST when you take it. The final bill shows the rest.\ntoConfirm:\n  - the notification number for the 5% rate\n  - the author's name and role\n---\n\n## What \"without input tax credit\" means\n\nAt 5% you can't take back the GST you paid on rent, products or equipment against the GST you charge. The 5% you collect goes to the government in full.\n\nBefore 22 Sep 2025, at 18%, salons could claim that credit.\n\n## Products you sell are taxed on their own\n\nShampoo, hair oil or a serum sold over the counter isn't a salon service. It goes on its own line with its HSN code and its own rate, not the 5% for services.\n\n## If you aren't registered\n\nBelow the turnover limit for services (₹20 lakh a year in most states, ₹10 lakh in some), you don't need to register, and you can't charge GST: your bill is a plain bill with no tax on it.\n",
